00:36:11.210 --> 00:36:13.290
it's three step process,

00:36:13.290 --> 00:36:19.530
as I mentioned, I think, Jim, you heard that from, Eastern Highland Health Districts as well.

00:36:20.090 --> 00:36:20.890
The first

00:36:22.410 --> 00:36:24.090
the first

00:36:24.255 --> 00:36:28.495
first process is, we submit plans to the state showing,

00:36:29.055 --> 00:36:33.375
what we're proposing for the property and where that where that well would be located.

00:36:34.015 --> 00:36:39.150
The state comes out to the property to get a sense of what's there currently,

00:36:39.550 --> 00:36:41.150
any adjacent wells,

00:36:41.470 --> 00:36:43.630
getting getting familiar with the neighborhood.

00:36:43.950 --> 00:36:45.150
So that's step one.

00:36:45.870 --> 00:36:46.830
Step two

00:36:47.150 --> 00:36:49.630
is the well is actually drilled.

00:36:50.190 --> 00:36:51.550
So during construction,

00:36:51.995 --> 00:36:53.515
a well is drilled,

00:36:54.075 --> 00:36:55.755
per the specifications,

00:36:56.155 --> 00:36:59.995
you know, of the public health code and installed on the property.

00:37:00.395 --> 00:37:03.435
Typically, this developer would be installing this well,

00:37:04.075 --> 00:37:04.955
alongside

00:37:04.955 --> 00:37:12.520
with other improvements to the property. The building would be being constructed. The, the pavement would be going in, drainage structures, other utilities.

00:37:13.160 --> 00:37:15.720
Step three of the process is once the,

00:37:15.960 --> 00:37:17.480
the well is drilled

00:37:17.720 --> 00:37:21.895
and connected to the proposed facility, then the water is tested.

00:37:22.215 --> 00:37:25.175
And depending on the results of that water,

00:37:25.495 --> 00:37:27.175
the water quality results,

00:37:27.335 --> 00:37:29.735
there may need to be some adjustments. So,

00:37:30.055 --> 00:37:30.775
historically,

00:37:31.015 --> 00:37:41.380
projects that I've been involved with, you get a clean result. There's nothing that needs to be done. The the health department will review the final paperwork and sign off. And,

00:37:41.780 --> 00:37:45.060
when the developer requests a certificate of occupancy,

00:37:45.220 --> 00:37:47.860
the building can be occupied and the water can be used.

00:37:48.260 --> 00:37:49.460
If during that testing,

00:37:50.075 --> 00:37:51.595
and this has happened before,

00:37:51.835 --> 00:37:52.555
there are some,

00:37:53.035 --> 00:37:53.755
elements,

00:37:54.155 --> 00:37:58.395
naturally occurring or maybe not naturally occurring that are found in the water supply,

00:37:58.795 --> 00:38:05.780
whether it be lead or arsenic or whatever it is, depending on what's found and at what concentration,

00:38:06.420 --> 00:38:06.820
the

00:38:07.300 --> 00:38:16.100
state may ask for a treatment system. And if that is required because of the water quality testing, then the developer would have to add a treatment system

00:38:16.340 --> 00:38:19.975
to the building so that when the water comes out the tap,

00:38:20.455 --> 00:38:24.775
for any customers or patrons to use, that it is safe to drink.

00:38:25.175 --> 00:38:26.855
That would need to be installed,

00:38:26.935 --> 00:38:28.055
retested,

00:38:28.055 --> 00:38:29.575
and to the satisfaction

00:38:29.575 --> 00:38:33.030
of the of the states. Once the state is satisfied,

00:38:33.110 --> 00:38:39.910
then, again, the developer could request a certificate of occupancy and the building could be occupied. So this is not a,

00:38:40.230 --> 00:38:43.430
I I can I won't be able to get you an approval

00:38:43.835 --> 00:38:50.715
prior to subdivision or prior to site plan approval? It's a very iterative ongoing process that

00:38:51.115 --> 00:38:54.475
can start as soon as we submit a site plan application,

00:38:54.795 --> 00:38:57.435
but literally will not end until

00:38:57.595 --> 00:38:58.795
things are constructed,

00:38:59.190 --> 00:39:03.190
well is connected to a sink and a sink is tested. So it's a very

00:39:03.430 --> 00:39:06.870
long process that spans the entire development of the property.

00:39:07.190 --> 00:39:10.950
But, what you guys should know and take a sense of comfort in is if,

00:39:11.750 --> 00:39:14.710
a well cannot be constructed or is not safe,

00:39:15.205 --> 00:39:16.005
then

00:39:17.365 --> 00:39:19.285
other agencies are involved

00:39:19.525 --> 00:39:20.245
and,

00:39:20.645 --> 00:39:24.005
nothing would open or be open to the public or used,

00:39:24.325 --> 00:39:28.245
business wouldn't be started until all of those criteria are met.

00:39:29.280 --> 00:39:31.200
It's a little bit more complicated,

00:39:31.440 --> 00:39:34.960
this process than for a single family residential home.

00:39:35.280 --> 00:39:36.960
That's why it goes to The States,

00:39:37.360 --> 00:39:39.760
and there's a lot of checks and balances along the way.

00:39:42.305 --> 00:39:47.265
That's kind of the the the process in a nutshell. I'm happy to answer any questions if that

00:39:48.225 --> 00:39:51.025
