>> Okay, we use GoToMeeting down here, so we don't use Zoom very often. So the statute is section eight dash 30 j which is part of the eight dash the famous eight dash 30 gs affordable

00:55:01.970 --> 00:55:03.170
housing statutes.

00:55:03.170 --> 00:55:05.650
The statute that was added in 2017

00:55:06.105 --> 00:55:10.025
is a dash 30 J eight dash 30 J entitled

00:55:10.025 --> 00:55:13.305
affordable housing plan hearing and adoption and amendments.

00:55:14.345 --> 00:55:16.905
What is causing all of this,

00:55:17.225 --> 00:55:19.385
all of these issues throughout Connecticut with

00:55:19.970 --> 00:55:21.730
consultants in towns

00:55:22.450 --> 00:55:25.250
wrangling trying to prepare affordable housing plans.

00:55:25.570 --> 00:55:35.250
And so what it really says is that at least once every five years each municipality shall prepare amend and adopt an affordable housing plan for the municipality.

00:55:35.945 --> 00:55:41.945
Such plans shall specify how the municipality intends to increase the number of affordable housing developments

00:55:42.105 --> 00:55:43.465
in the municipality.

00:55:44.025 --> 00:55:50.230
And that is it. You have no other guidance than that. That's the only thing. Those two sentences

00:55:50.390 --> 00:55:52.870
is what has caused all of this situation.

00:55:53.750 --> 00:56:20.090
They could have just added it to a part of a plan of conservation and development and then next, when you do your plan of conservation development, that part of it is an affordable housing, but they felt it was so important that they wanted to put it into a public act. And they put those two sentences in. So those two sentences are causing every town in Connecticut to have to work on preparing an affordable housing plan, whether it's Union Connecticut, Andover Connecticut or Bridgeport Connecticut. We're

00:56:20.090 --> 00:56:21.290
all in the same boat,

00:56:21.530 --> 00:56:28.090
which causes a lot of problems in Connecticut because we are so diverse and whether you know it's Greenwich or Bridgeport

00:56:28.345 --> 00:56:32.185
both have to look at affordable housing and how to address the issue. So

00:56:33.305 --> 00:56:37.705
there's a lot of concerns I think that we'll get into and how it affects Andover,

00:56:38.345 --> 00:56:40.185
but that is the only

00:56:40.825 --> 00:56:54.560
guidance that we have. So really we can look at it as well, there's no guidance on how we're supposed to do this, or we can look at it and say well okay and now the state has given us money to do this, this opens up an opportunity to do some good stuff, some good investigation into

00:56:55.625 --> 00:57:02.425
Andover really needs. As you know, I've been working with Andover for I was working with them for about ten years.

00:57:03.305 --> 00:57:07.545
And off five years as a as a as your planner and five years as a consultant

00:57:07.920 --> 00:57:17.040
And we did different things and we have various sections of affordable housing that we talked about. We did an incentive housing plan, we have that

00:57:17.200 --> 00:57:19.840
so we have some some good information certainly

00:57:19.840 --> 00:57:22.560
from the incentive housing plan which will certainly be used

00:57:22.995 --> 00:57:26.115
That was only five years ago and not

00:57:26.435 --> 00:57:31.635
a lot has changed in Annover so that will be used. We're not totally reinventing the wheel.

00:57:32.035 --> 00:57:33.155
But back to the statute,

00:57:34.830 --> 00:57:43.390
the municipality may hold a public informational meeting or other activities to inform residents about the process in May. So you are not even required

00:57:44.430 --> 00:58:04.320
to have a public hearing to adopt this affordable housing plan. So you don't have to have a public hearing, you can adopt it. It doesn't have to be the Planning and Zoning Commission that is doing it. It could be in a lot of towns it's the Board of Selectmen that are overseeing it and are adopting it. That's what's happening here in Middlefield where I live is the Board of Selectmen have almost exclusively

00:58:04.320 --> 00:58:08.800
run the show same in Durham and Haddam where I work.

00:58:09.280 --> 00:58:14.240
The Planning and Zoning Commission will be doing it, which I think is the right way to do it and so I agree with what you're doing.

00:58:15.775 --> 00:58:17.855
But again, no real guidance.

00:58:17.935 --> 00:58:20.095
If you want to change your zoning to add

00:58:21.295 --> 00:58:25.855
some little section, you have to have a whole public hearing. Here, you don't have to have a public hearing.

00:58:27.180 --> 00:58:31.820
The statute goes on to say you must review the plan and amend it every five years.

00:58:32.700 --> 00:58:39.660
So this is so you'll be back looking at this in five years from June 30, so in 2027,

00:58:39.915 --> 00:58:43.995
you'll be looking at it again saying we have to update the affordable housing plan.

00:58:45.755 --> 00:58:51.355
One of the big problems in Connecticut is there's no teeth to these things so just like the planet conservation and development

00:58:52.040 --> 00:58:57.240
The only real teeth and the plan of conservation development has a little more teeth now

00:58:57.400 --> 00:59:00.440
about discretionary funding and holding money back.

00:59:01.400 --> 00:59:13.935
The real only penalty for not having an affordable housing plan if you don't do this is that you have to send a letter to the state saying to State Department of Housing that we did not adopt an affordable housing plan and this is why.

00:59:15.615 --> 00:59:17.535
That's the only thing you have to do.

00:59:17.855 --> 00:59:21.775
The one thing there's a grant out right now that

00:59:21.370 --> 00:59:31.370
they're getting a little more serious about it that you have to fill out a form to say that you are not in compliance with updating your plan of conservation and development and your affordable housing plan.

00:59:32.090 --> 00:59:33.530
